      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I am so sorry you are feeling this way; the silence after a beloved pet leaves often feels deafening and empty, even when we tell ourselves to \"be strong.\" It is completely normal to feel a deep sense of purposelessness and despair, as the home no longer serves its familiar function without them. Please give yourself permission to grieve in your own way without judgment, and consider reaching out to a support group or counselor to help you navigate this profound grief.",
